            "result_text": "Done! I've created `/app/run.py` with the `run_tasks` function.\n\nHow it works:\n- **`asyncio.Semaphore`** limits how many tasks run concurrently by forcing each task to acquire/release the semaphore before/after execution\n- **`asyncio.gather()`** waits for all wrapped tasks to complete\n- **Cleanup on interrupt**: When you hit Ctrl+C, asyncio cancels pending tasks, but running tasks still execute their `finally` blocks and async context manager cleanup code (`__aexit__`)\n\nYou can use it like:\n```python\nimport asyncio\nfrom run import run_tasks\n\nasync def task1():\n    try:\n        # work\n    finally:\n        # cleanup always runs\n        pass\n\nawait run_tasks([task1, task2, task3], max_concurrent=5)\n```"
